  "notModeled": [
    "analog front end, input ranges (RANGE_CHn stored only; the 0 V code is 20000h, the bipolar default range's straight-binary mid-scale; unipolar ranges would give 00000h)",
    "power-up idle state: the device converts nothing until the first AUTO_RST/MAN command (modeled: every CS fall converts)",
    "RST mode after a reset converts nothing until AUTO_RST/MAN (modeled: conversions continue)",
    "AUTO_RST channel sequencing over AUTO_SEQ_EN (modeled: AUTO_RST selects channel 0 and stays there); CH_PWR_DN stored only",
    "SDO formats 001-011 (channel address, device address and range bits appended after the result); only format 000 (16 result bits then low) is shifted",
    "ALARM feature: thresholds, hysteresis, tripped/active flags and the ALARM pin (pin 35 is never driven; the 0 V code is inside the default thresholds FFFFh/0000h on the top 16 bits so no alarm would trip)",
    "daisy-chain mode (DAISY input shifted through SDO) and DEV ID bits",
    "RST/PD pin pulse width: < 100 ns low = register reset, >= 400 ns = power-down; modeled as a reset held while low",
    "STDBY vs PWR_DN wake-up times (both modeled as power-down left by AUTO_RST/MAN)",
    "program register writes take effect at the next CS fall (modeled: at CS rise of the write frame)",
    "SDO during the 16 bits of a command frame is 0 for every frame type; invalid data returned in RST mode with 32 SCLKs",
    "REFSEL internal/external reference selection (analog)",
    "SCLK frequency limit (18 MHz; the 16th SCLK falling edge must come after tCONV 825 ns)",
    "SDO data-change delay is not specified (only hold 10 ns and setup 25 ns at tSCLK 56 ns); tOut uses the 10 ns hold time"
  ],
  "variants": "ADS8694: 4-channel, pins 12-15 and 24-27 NC, the channel 4-7 bits and registers read as 1s and ignore writes. ADS8698: 8-channel. 18-bit versions of the ADS8684A/ADS8688A with the same register map and commands.",
